ar phylogenetics at the Felsenstein zone: approaching the <italic>Strepsiptera</italic> problem using 5.8S and 28S rDNA sequences</article-title><source>Mol Phylogenet Evol</source><year>1998</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>470</fpage><lpage>480</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9667995</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b124"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hypsa</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parasite histories and novel phylogenetic tools: alternative approaches to inferring parasite evolution from molecular markers</article-title><source>Int J Parasitol</source><year>2006</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>141</fpage><lpage>155</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16387305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b125"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ishikawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evolution of ribosomal RNA</article-title><source>Comp Biochem Physiol B</source><year>1977</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">400949</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b126"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ishikawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studies of thermal conversion of 28S RNA of <italic>Galleria mellonella</italic> (L.) to an 18S product</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>1972</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>144</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5015395</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b127"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Israelewski</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure and function of an AT-rich, interspersed repetitive sequence from <italic>Chironomus thummi</italic>: solenoidal DNA, 142 bp palindro